cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "RL IoT Defense System: Adversarial Reinforcement Learning for
  Kill-Chain-Aware IoT Defense"
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Felipe
    family-names: Santos
    affiliation: "MSc Thesis"
abstract: >-
  An adversarial reinforcement learning framework for IoT network defense over
  the CICIoT2023 dataset. The system pairs an LSTM-based attack sequence
  generator (Red Team) with RL defense agents (Blue Team) that learn graduated
  force-continuum policies. Inspired by IoTWarden (Alam et al., 2024), this
  project extends the original work with realistic feature observations, a
  five-level force continuum, and a kill-chain abstraction grounded in real
  CICIoT2023 traffic.
keywords:
  - reinforcement-learning
  - intrusion-detection
  - iot-security
  - kill-chain
  - adversarial-rl
  - lstm
  - ciciot2023
